1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:10,320
This October, gold is trading above four thousand dollars an ounce. And one cheap metal weighs almost exactly the same. Tungsten.

2
00:00:10,595 --> 00:00:21,575
Now picture this. You find a one-ounce gold bar online, two hundred dollars under spot. Sealed. A serial number. A five-star seller. You tap buy.

3
00:00:21,810 --> 00:00:29,270
It arrives. The weight checks out. A magnet won't stick. But under a thin skin of gold, it's tungsten.

4
00:00:29,665 --> 00:00:34,565
So who takes the loss? Not the seller. They're gone. You.

5
00:00:34,890 --> 00:00:40,550
You paid three thousand, nine hundred and sixty-five dollars. What you're holding is worth almost nothing.

6
00:00:40,905 --> 00:00:54,925
And it isn't just online. In twenty twelve, a jeweler in Manhattan's Diamond District paid a hundred thousand dollars for four ten-ounce gold bars. Serial numbers. Paperwork. Filled with tungsten.

7
00:00:55,320 --> 00:01:00,960
Meanwhile, deals that look this good get listed every day. Quietly. With great reviews.

8
00:01:01,335 --> 00:01:05,075
So, do you really know what's inside your gold?

9
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:14,360
Don't worry. At Bullion Trading, we never just assume a bar is genuine. We test it in front of you at our New York counter, and before anything ships.

10
00:01:14,735 --> 00:01:18,575
From your next bar on, we've got you. Buy from Bullion Trading.
